  {
    "client_msg_id": "18aa8cb8-4dc4-4dde-bb3e-db927cb4d9b1",
    "type": "message",
    "user": "U08S0TP9R3P",
    "text": "Hi \u003c@U0A5EGHRLQY\u003e thanks for flagging this. We've identified the root cause, the source table has a BLOB column `name: blob`, and our MySQL connector currently treats BLOB column as plain text instead of raw binary data. Since these columns can contain bytes that aren't valid UTF-8 text, the sync fails when writing to Iceberg.\n\nWe already have a fix in progress \u003chttps://github.com/datazip-inc/olake/pull/1183|(PR #1183)\u003e that adds proper binary type support end-to-end . We'll share an ETA shortly. Thanks!",
    "ts": "1789548236.731839",
    "thread_ts": "1789544973.908769",
